{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/647710-what-kind-of-spirits-are-you-likely-to-find-in-the-abyss","id":647710,"title":"What kind of spirits are you likely to find in the Abyss?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-31T23:41:12-07:00","id":647710,"title":"What kind of spirits are you likely to find in the Abyss?","content":"The Abyss has a multitude of spirits dormant in it, but some are likely to be more common than others. Spirits of concepts that have become less popular and of forests that no longer exist. What sort of examples would you expect to see in the Abyss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T01:36:30-07:00","id":647777,"title":"","content":"I would put a large vacant mall full of all the stores of yesteryear that have long since closed (York steakhouse anyone?) and a parking lot that stretch's to the horizon with old outdated cars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T01:42:27-07:00","id":647779,"title":"","content":"Night, Shadow, Darkness, Fear should be quite ubiquitous. I've actually had a giant kingdom of Shadow inspired by the City of Brass in one of the tunnels where the Bubasti went to commune with them and learn magicks pertaining to darkness. I've also got a pet theory that whatever is summoned by Obtenebration is a Thing that exists in the endless caves and tunnels on the canyons and that it writhes and slithers through them trying to smother everything in its inky blackness.<br /> <br /> I also play up that The Abyss is a place where you can actually find endless lost and forgotten things. From photographs to tombstones and weapons. Occasionally you might even find things that you really wish that stayed forgotten. There was this very natural progression of an Ananasi PC facing off the ghost of the person who he ate to take his place and then binding him into the weapon he used to kill him and tossing it into the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Planescape's Pandemonium is also nice inspiration for the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:53:01-07:00","id":648031,"title":"","content":"I was going to comment examples, but Dwight and Asmodai did a good job, soooo.... &quot;likes&quot; for them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T00:49:42-07:00","id":648634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/647710-what-kind-of-spirits-are-you-likely-to-find-in-the-abyss?p=647779#post647779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Night, Shadow, Darkness, Fear should be quite ubiquitous.</div> </div> </div> </div>So these are the types of spirits that should be their? And if so, are these spirits Wyrm corrupted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/647710-what-kind-of-spirits-are-you-likely-to-find-in-the-abyss?p=647779#post647779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also play up that The Abyss is a place where you can actually find endless lost and forgotten things. From photographs to tombstones and weapons. Occasionally you might even find things that you really wish that stayed forgotten. There was this very natural progression of an Ananasi PC facing off the ghost of the person who he ate to take his place and then binding him into the weapon he used to kill him and tossing it into the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was this the real Wraith or just some sort of emanation that represents the man?<br /> <br /> Edit: And do the objects come from the physical world, or are they projections?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-02-2015, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T00:56:23-07:00","id":648647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/647710-what-kind-of-spirits-are-you-likely-to-find-in-the-abyss?p=648634#post648634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So these are the types of spirits that should be their? And if so, are these spirits Wyrm corrupted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some might be others not, the more you treat the spirit life in the abyss as some deep sea life the better you are. These are discarded or even aborted spirits some are barely concepts of things. Think alien and strange let your players minds fill in the blanks it will be far more creepy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T12:39:05-07:00","id":651650,"title":"","content":"There's also some incredibly powerful garou there, as well as bunyip. Spirals are having some inter pack troubles (as of umbra 20th), so you could &quot;align&quot; with one to kill another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}